\id PSA  
\h Psalms 
\toc1 PSALMS 
\toc2 Psalms 
\toc3 PSA 
\mt1 PSALMS  
\c 10  
\d (11 in KJV) For the end, a Psalm of David.  
\q1
\v 1 In the Lord I have put my trust: how will you⌃ say to my soul,   
\q1
\v 2 Flee to the mountains as a sparrow?   
\q1
\v 3 For behold the sinners have bent their \add bow\add*, they have prepared their arrows for the quiver, to shoot \f + \fr 10:3 \fl Gr. \ft in dark moon, or little moonlight, \fl q. d. \ft luce malignâ \f*privily at the upright in heart.   
\q1
\v 4 For they have pulled down what you did frame, but what has the righteous done?   
\q1
\v 5 The Lord is in his holy temple, as for the Lord, his throne is in heaven: his eyes look upon the poor, his eyelids try the sons of men.   
\q1
\v 6 The Lord tries the righteous and the ungodly: and he that loves unrighteousness hates his own soul.   
\q1
\v 7 He shall rain upon sinners snares, fire, and brimstone, and a stormy blast \add shall be\add* the portion of their cup.   
\q1
\v 8 For the Lord \add is\add* righteous, and loves \f + \fr 10:8 \fl Gr. \ft righteousnesses\f*righteousness; his face beholds uprightness.   
\c 114  
\d (115)  
\q1
\v 1 Not to us, O Lord, not to us, but to your name give glory, because of your mercy and your truth;   
\q1
\v 2 lest at any time the nations should say, Where is their God?   
\q1
\v 3 But our God has done in heaven and on earth, whatever he has pleased.   
\q1
\v 4 The idols of the nations are silver and gold, the works of men's hands.   
\q1
\v 5 They have a mouth, but they \f + \fr 114:5 \fl Gr. \ft will not. \f* can’t speak; they have eyes, but they can’t see:   
\q1
\v 6 they have ears, but they can’t hear; they have noses, but they can’t smell;   
\q1
\v 7 they have hands, but they can’t handle; they have feet, but they can’t walk: they can’t speak through their throat.   
\q1
\v 8 Let those that make them become like to them, and all who trust in them.   
\q1
\v 9 The house of Israel trusts in the Lord: he is their helper and defender.   
\q1
\v 10 The house of Aaron trusts in the Lord: he is their helper and defender.   
\q1
\v 11 They that fear the Lord trust in the Lord: he is their helper and defender.   
\q1
\v 12 The Lord has remembered us, and blessed us: he has blessed the house of Israel, he has blessed the house of Aaron.   
\q1
\v 13 He has blessed them that fear the Lord, both small and great.   
\q1
\v 14 The Lord \f + \fr 114:14 \fl Or, \ft increase you. \f* add \add blessings\add* to you and to your children.   
\q1
\v 15 Blessed are you⌃ of the Lord, who made the heaven and the earth.   
\q1
\v 16 The heaven of \f + \fr 114:16 \fl Gr. \ft sing. \f* heavens \add belongs\add* to the Lord: but he has given the earth to the sons of men.   
\q1
\v 17 The dead shall not praise you, O Lord, nor any that go down to Hades.   
\q1
\v 18 But we, the living, will bless the Lord, from henceforth and for ever.   
\c 115  
\d (116) Alleluia.  
\q1
\v 1 I am well pleased, because the Lord will listen to the voice of my supplication.   
\q1
\v 2 Because he has inclined his ear to me, therefore will I call upon him while I live.   
\q1
\v 3 The pangs of death compassed me; the dangers of hell found me: I found affliction and sorrow.   
\q1
\v 4 Then I called on the name of the Lord: O Lord, deliver my soul.   
\q1
\v 5 The Lord is merciful and righteous; yes, our God has pity.   
\q1
\v 6 The Lord preserves \f + \fr 115:6 \fl Gr. \ft infants. \f* the simple: I was brought low, and he delivered me.   
\q1
\v 7 Return to your rest, O my soul; for the Lord has dealt bountifully with you.   
\q1
\v 8 For he has delivered my soul from death, my eyes from tears, and my feet from falling.   
\q1
\v 9 I shall be well-pleasing before the Lord in the land of the living.  
\d (115) Alleluia.   
\q1
\v 10 \f + \fr 115:10 \ft In Brenton's text, Psalm 115 commences here, but verse numbers continue from v10 to v19. \f* \x + \xo 115:10 \xt 2 Cor 4:13 \x* I believed, therefore I have spoken: but I was greatly afflicted.   
\q1
\v 11 And I said in my amazement, Every man is a liar.   
\q1
\v 12 What shall I render to the Lord for all the things wherein he has rewarded me?   
\q1
\v 13 I will take the cup of salvation, and call upon the name of the Lord.   
\q1
\v 14 I will pay my vows to the Lord, in the presence of all his people.   
\q1
\v 15 Precious in the sight of the Lord is the death of his saints.   
\q1
\v 16 O Lord, I am your servant; I am your servant, and the son of your handmaid: you have burst my bonds asunder.   
\q1
\v 17 I will offer to you the sacrifice of praise, and will call upon the name of the Lord.   
\q1
\v 18 I will pay my vows to the Lord, in the presence of all his people,   
\q1
\v 19 in the courts of the Lord's house, in the midst of you, Jerusalem.   
